ven-names></name><name><surname>van der Kaay</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The El Ni&#x000f1;o Southern Oscillation and the Historic Malaria Epidemics on the Indian Subcontinent and Sri Lanka: An Early Warning System for Future Epidemics?</article-title><source>Trop Med &#x00026; Internat Health</source><year>1996</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>86</fpage><lpage>96</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nash</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><source>El Nino: Unlocking the Secrets of the Master Weather-maker</source><year>2002</year><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Warner</publisher-name><fpage>168</fpage><lpage>179</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Todd</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Washington</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheke</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Brown locust outbreaks and climate variability in southern Africa</article-title><source>J Applied Ecology</source><year>2002</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>42</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Red tides during spring 1998 in Hong Kong: is El Ni&#x000f1;o responsible?</article-title><source>Mar Ecol Prog Ser</source><year>1999</year><volume>187</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>294</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Poveda</s